<title>HUNGARY: MOL SHARES OPEN HIGHER ON 1996 RESULTS.</title>
<headline>MOL SHARES OPEN HIGHER ON 1996 RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>MOL shares opened sharply higher on Friday following the release of 1996 preliminary IAS results this morning showing net income soaring to 22.2 billion forints in 1996 compared with 1.1 billion forints in 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;This was the company's best year ever,&quot; MOL's CEO Zoltan Mandoki told a news conference.</p>
<p>MOL opened at 3,200 forints after closing Thursday at 3,095.</p>
<p>Analysts said earlier MOL's profit was 10 billion forints better than the market expected.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (361) 327 4040</p>
